   "rule_summary": "Manufacturers must report any thermal runaway, fire, smoke event, or overheating incident involving a unit to the responsible regulator within 24 hours of learning of it, including incidents involving injury, property damage, or no apparent harm. The manufacturer must notify the affected customer within 24 hours when the event involves their unit, and promptly provide safety instructions.",
   "comparison": "all parameters acceptable or better",
   "final_rule_text": "Manufacturers must report any thermal runaway, fire, smoke event, or overheating incident involving a unit to the responsible regulator within 24 hours of learning of it, including incidents involving injury, property damage, or no apparent harm. They must provide a complete investigation and corrective-action update within 30 days, or explain why more time is needed. The manufacturer must notify the affected customer within 24 hours when the event involves their unit, and promptly provide safety instructions. If a hazard may affect other customers or the public, notify regulators and potentially affected customers within 24 hours and issue interim precautions. Keep an auditable incident log and report all incidents; suspected under-reporting must be disclosed and corrected."
  },
