   "comparison": "all parameters acceptable or better",
   "final_rule_text": "New home battery systems must provide a secure remote emergency shut-off capability that can be activated by the customer and, where an imminent safety hazard warrants it, by the manufacturer or responsible emergency authority under documented procedures. Manufacturers must provide clear instructions and maintain safeguards against unauthorized activation. For installed units, manufacturers must enable or retrofit remote shut-off within 72 months of adoption where technically feasible; where it is not feasible, they must notify the owner, explain the limitation, and provide an alternative emergency isolation method and instructions. Remote shut-off must not replace required physical safety protections."
