   "rule_summary": "If any model exceeds 8 thermal incidents per 100,000 installed units in that period, the manufacturer must promptly report the exceedance to the regulator, initiate corrective action, and conduct a mandatory recall of that model. Notices must promptly reach known owners and be accessible to neighbours and the public, and explain the hazard, affected units, immediate precautions, and remedy.",
   "comparison": "all parameters acceptable or better",
   "final_rule_text": "Before purchase, customers must receive clear written information on installation, safe operation, emergency response, maintenance, and how to report an incident. Notify affected customers promptly of material newly identified safety risks and provide practical precautions and remedies. For each model, thermal incidents per 100,000 installed units must be calculated using a consistent incident basis and installed-unit denominator over a rolling 12-month period. If any model exceeds 8 thermal incidents per 100,000 installed units in that period, the manufacturer must promptly report the exceedance to the regulator, initiate corrective action, and conduct a mandatory recall of that model. Notices must promptly reach known owners and be accessible to neighbours and the public, and explain the hazard, affected units, immediate precautions, and remedy."
